Central Enterprises Inc.
Application for Retail Liquor License
Executive Summary
Vision
As the holder of a City of Cheyenne Retail Liquor License, Central Enterprises Inc.will
Cheyenne business district.The establishment will be a place of high activity andwill be
seafood, salads, and other unique food styles.
We will offer a product based on a chef-inspired menu, and high quality private dining
rooms for consumers and businesses.We will serve as a premier community gathering
establishment.In addition to high-endcasual dining, customers will enjoy our tavern,
package liquor, catering, and private dining services.
About Central Enterprises
Central Enterprises Inc.isa Wyoming Corporation, in good standing and established in
August 2007 (Attachment A).
Financing
The project is being financed through private investment and a line of credit loan facility
provided by Wyoming Bank&Trust(WB&T).Please see letter of good standing from
·WB&T(Attachment B).
Lease
Central Enterprises will lease9, ooo square feet including the main floor and basement
located at the historic corner of17th Street and Carey Avenue(1701Carey)indowntown
Cheyenne.Please see Attachment C for the formal property legal description.The
building is owned by Otis Investments, LLC (Lessor).Arenovation of the building
lease will expressly permit the sale of alcoholic beverages(Attachment G).
Benefits to Downtown Cheyenne
·Historical Building Renovation-The project is the foundation for returning this
building to its former glory.The building exterior will be restored to its original Art
Moderne style with white matte finish terracotta tiles as described in the National
Register of Historic Places.
Economic Boost-Increased foot traffic generated by the project willbenefit
neighboring retail businesses.
·Social Boost-The new establishment will draw customers from abroad range of
ages and demographic groups. In turn, this will bring social benefits to the
downtown Cheyenne community.
Serve As An Anchor-Renovation of the existing building and development of a
thriving business will create motivation for further development in the immediate
area.
Enhanced Services-Private dining and catering are seriously under served in
downtown Cheyenne and throughout the broader Cheyenne community.
o Private Dining-There are very limited opportunities for private dining
facilities offered by similar existing businesses, with the only option being
Central Enterprises Inc.
Application for Retail Liquor License
